#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:5
#: d81dd794af1241d3b7201974de10bd29
msgid "Motor Thrust Scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:7
#: 17e76a0ed43f4ceb962c80e49d04d398
msgid "Copter includes *motor thrust scaling* which compensates for the non-linear thrust output of most ESCs and motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:12
#: e67d3860832a475cabc12979be46590e
msgid "The default curve should work for nearly all ESC/motor combinations. Normally the parameters should not be adjusted unless the vehicle’s actual thrust curve has been measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:17
#: 3d5af5250ad241c683a7764ffaf62b7c
msgid "Thrust Curves"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:19
#: 721aeedd4e6e4393a3304b1270063cb3
msgid "The curve is controlled by two parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:21
#: af4ede2a9fff4898827dc7b6195e0da8
msgid ":ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO<MOT_THST_EXPO>` controls the shape of the thrust curve with \"0\" meaning a completely linear curve and \"1.0\" being very curved (see pictures below).  The default is \"0.65\" (the image below incorrectly states the default is 0.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:26
#: 6477ea30f7b84a09ab54ebfe2d571ec5
msgid "Some ESCs have built-in linearizing curves and the default EXPO value of \"0.65\" will cause stability issues, requiring thrust stand measurements to adjust the EXPO. Typically, values of \"0\" to \"0.2\" will result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:31
#: 296fda81be5249f0a98953e24e80894f
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MAX<MOT_SPIN_MAX>` controls the point at which the thrust flattens out near its maximum.  By default this is 0.95 meaning 95% of full throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:36
#: 0c7c6a6783364055907f154c21d82000
msgid "Thrust Stands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:38
#: b43b42b92abb43a5805db8921b4cc7b4
msgid "The thrust stands listed below can be used to measure the PWM signal vs thrust output for a vehicle's specific motor, esc and battery. Be sure to use the ESCs rated input PWM range when measuring these values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:40
#: 43a0c1da85dd49c48c8b670293005400
msgid "`RCbenchmark.com thrust stands <https://www.rcbenchmark.com/pages/series-1580-thrust-stand-dynamometer>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:41
#: f39346a7255b434586587d61b4ff5d5b
msgid "`Turnigy thrust stand <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-thrust-stand-and-power-analyser-v3.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:44
#: 6b739f38e425455780371df5c09bee8c
msgid "Parameter Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:46
#: c09e5427e69f45b0b504f880f2ccfb05
msgid "The WebTool: `ArduPilot Thrust Expo <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/WebTools/ThrustExpo/>`__ can be used to calculate the appropriate values from the thrust stand data above."
msgstr ""
